DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ggeettggiidd() system call returns the real group ID of the calling
     process, ggeetteeggiidd() returns the effective group ID of the calling process.

     The real group ID is specified at login time.

     The real group ID is the group of the user who invoked the program.  As
     the effective group ID gives the process additional permissions during
     the execution of “_s_e_t_-_g_r_o_u_p_-_I_D” mode processes, ggeettggiidd() is used to de‐
     termine the real-user-id of the calling process.

EERRRROORRSS
     The ggeettggiidd() and ggeetteeggiidd() system calls are always successful, and no re‐
     turn value is reserved to indicate an error.

